cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its methodology, please cite the accompanying paper (preferred) or this repository."
type: software
title: "quant-trading-agent: a falsification-first research framework for quantitative strategy selection"
abstract: >-
  A triad closed-loop research framework for quantitative strategies:
  proponent (exploration / code-level optimisation) x adversary (risk register plus
  executable optimisation prescriptions) x neutral judge (independent re-runs, G1-G11
  admission gates, F0-F6 forward-first anti-self-deception audit, D0-D4 pre-deployment
  code audit with a SHA256 fingerprint). Includes an injected-truth evaluation protocol
  with a random-admission control, and the experiments behind the accompanying paper.
authors:
  - family-names: "Zheng"
    given-names: "Tianlun"
    affiliation: "Fudan University"
version: "2.2.1"
date-released: "2026-10-06"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/simplify23/quant-trading-agent"
url: "https://github.com/simplify23/quant-trading-agent"
keywords:
  - "quantitative finance"
  - "multiple testing"
  - "backtest overfitting"
  - "deflated Sharpe ratio"
  - "false discovery rate"
  - "strategy admission"
  - "research methodology"
  - "replication crisis"
  - "injected-truth validation"
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "On the Boundary of Admission Gates: An Injected-Truth Study of Falsification-First Selection in Quantitative Strategy Research"
  abstract: >-
    Strategy research conflates two problems: finding a profitable rule, and establishing
    that the finding is not search luck. We introduce an injected-truth protocol with a
    random-admission control, and show across synthetic and real-calibrated panels that
    admission gates eliminate false discoveries in the weak-signal regime but cut adoption
    to 1-7%, add nothing when signals are strong, and silently reject every candidate when
    criteria are computed on absolute rather than excess returns.
  authors:
    - family-names: "Zheng"
      given-names: "Tianlun"
      affiliation: "Fudan University"
  year: 2026
